. In the instant petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution, the petitioners have prayed for the following reliefs:
i) By issuance of a 'Writ of Mandamus', or any other appropriate Writ, Order or direction, the Respondents be directed to handover the possession of the land measuring 03 Kanals and 17 Marlas falling under Survey No.771 and 02 Kanals and 10 Marlas covered under Survey No. 766 situate in Mouzai Zewan, Pantha Chowk,
Srinagar to the Petitioners forthwith, along with mesne profits with respect thereto;
ii) By issuance of a 'Writ of Mandamus', or any other appropriate Writ, Order or direction, the Respondents be directed to pay compensation in favour of the Petitioners for the illegal occupation of their aforesaid property for decades;
iii) By issuance of a 'Writ of Prohibition, or any other appropriate Writ, Order or direction, the Respondents be prohibited from transferring the aforesaid landed property of the Petitioners to the Ghulam Mohammad Wani And Others vs Government Of J&K And Others
